<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- MANY_WATERS_DRILL_BUILDINGS_1 — which of Ash'karr's maps yield a drillable
       liquid, wired as DATA, same shape as ManyWaters_RiverSteam_Ashkarr.xml.

       FlowWorks (RimMandrake.FlowWorks.Drilling.RM_SubsurfaceLiquidBiomeExtension)
       is a RimMandrake-tier engine and names no biome of its own — which biome
       drills, for what, and how richly is campaign wiring, and campaign wiring
       lives here, exactly like river steam.

       RM_FE_Pyrelands (mandrake.rm.pyrelands) is the Pyrelands biome the frozen
       world actually carries — 222 tiles, MEASURED live 2026-09-19. The second
       operation below is the one that does the work on the shipped world.
       ZBiome_Grasslands is zylle's More Vanilla Biomes grassland, still labelled
       "the Pyrelands" by BiomeNames_Ashkarr.xml but carrying ZERO tiles on the
       canonical planet; it is patched too, conditionally, and costs nothing.

       Two candidate liquids, both already shipped with a canal form
       (LiquidDef.canalFluid) so a drill striking either can actually pour:
         - RM_Liquid_FreshWater (RM_Fluid_Water) — the common case. The
           excavation engine's ActiveFluid defaults to water on any map that
           has not otherwise committed to something else, so a fresh-water
           drill works out of the box with no other setup (see
           Building_LiquidDrill's own doc comment on the one-fluid-per-map
           limitation).
         - RM_Liquid_Tar (RM_Fluid_Tar) — "Tar needs the viscosity most of
           all" (owner ruling, 2026-09-16). A tar drill on a map whose
           channels are not ALREADY running tar (e.g. via the debug
           ActiveFluid switch) produces nothing rather than mixing two
           liquids the engine has no model for — a disclosed limitation, not
           a bug, until true multi-fluid maps ship.

       Gated twice, both deliberately (same reasoning as the river-steam
       patch): PatchOperationFindMod so a cut FlowWorks makes this a no-op
       rather than leaving a dangling modExtension reference, and
       PatchOperationConditional on the biome def so a missing More Vanilla
       Biomes does not throw against a missing xpath. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: FlowWorks</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
        <!-- ManyWaters_RiverSteam_Ashkarr.xml already checked this file has no
             native <modExtensions> as of 2026-09-08, and its own patch (which
             loads before this one, same PatchOperationFindMod gate) has since
             ADDED one via the nomatch branch below — so by the time this
             patch runs, <modExtensions> exists whenever FlowWorks is active.
             Checked again here rather than assumed, because a second
             <modExtensions> element is not a merge: the loader keeps one and
             silently drops the other's contents. -->
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/modExtensions</xpath>
        <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/modExtensions</xpath>
          <value>
            <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.Drilling.RM_SubsurfaceLiquidBiomeExtension">
              <chanceMapHasYield>0.6</chanceMapHasYield>
              <options>
                <li>
                  <liquid>RM_Liquid_FreshWater</liquid>
                  <commonality>3</commonality>
                  <reserveUnits>600~1800</reserveUnits>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <liquid>RM_Liquid_Tar</liquid>
                  <commonality>1</commonality>
                  <reserveUnits>400~1200</reserveUnits>
                </li>
              </options>
            </li>
          </value>
        </match>
        <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <modExtensions>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.Drilling.RM_SubsurfaceLiquidBiomeExtension">
                <chanceMapHasYield>0.6</chanceMapHasYield>
                <options>
                  <li>
                    <liquid>RM_Liquid_FreshWater</liquid>
                    <commonality>3</commonality>
                    <reserveUnits>600~1800</reserveUnits>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <liquid>RM_Liquid_Tar</liquid>
                    <commonality>1</commonality>
                    <reserveUnits>400~1200</reserveUnits>
                  </li>
                </options>
              </li>
            </modExtensions>
          </value>
        </nomatch>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>


  <!-- 🔴 RM_FE_Pyrelands is the biome the FROZEN WORLD actually carries.
       MEASURED live 2026-09-19 (FOUNDRY bridge wave 2) on the canonical planet
       (seed "raven", coverage 1.0, jawa/world_tile_export over 21872 surface
       tiles): 222 tiles are BiomeDef RM_FE_Pyrelands and ZERO are
       ZBiome_Grasslands. The Pyrelands live in mandrake.rm.pyrelands now; the
       operation above was copied from the river-steam patch, which had the same
       stale target, so no map on the shipped world could ever roll a subsurface
       yield. Both defNames are patched and each operation is conditional on its
       def existing, so patching a biome with no tiles costs nothing. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: FlowWorks</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/modExtensions</xpath>
        <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/modExtensions</xpath>
          <value>
            <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.Drilling.RM_SubsurfaceLiquidBiomeExtension">
                <chanceMapHasYield>0.6</chanceMapHasYield>
                <options>
                  <li>
                    <liquid>RM_Liquid_FreshWater</liquid>
                    <commonality>3</commonality>
                    <reserveUnits>600~1800</reserveUnits>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <liquid>RM_Liquid_Tar</liquid>
                    <commonality>1</commonality>
                    <reserveUnits>400~1200</reserveUnits>
                  </li>
                </options>
              </li>
          </value>
        </match>
        <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <modExtensions>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.Drilling.RM_SubsurfaceLiquidBiomeExtension">
                <chanceMapHasYield>0.6</chanceMapHasYield>
                <options>
                  <li>
                    <liquid>RM_Liquid_FreshWater</liquid>
                    <commonality>3</commonality>
                    <reserveUnits>600~1800</reserveUnits>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <liquid>RM_Liquid_Tar</liquid>
                    <commonality>1</commonality>
                    <reserveUnits>400~1200</reserveUnits>
                  </li>
                </options>
              </li>
            </modExtensions>
          </value>
        </nomatch>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
